LL call sites through it. `grep 'get_or_create_collection(\"knowledge\")'`\n23\t   must return nothing.\n24\t2. **No triples → empty graph.** Documents page's kg3d/synoptic_web reads Neo4j (`graph/kg3d/ontology.py`),\n25\t   populated only by `deep_synthesis` (triple extraction). But Bridge `ingest()` posted `{workspace}` and\n26\t   `deep_synthesis` defaults False → graph stayed empty though the chip promises triples.\n27\t   **FIX:** `bridge.js ingest()` now sends `deep_synthesis:true`.\n28\t3. **Silent failure.** Indexing/synthesis errors caught + reported as success.\n29\t   **FIX:** ingest tracks per-file `indexed`/`error`, returns honest `status` ∈ completed /\n30\t   completed_with_errors / failed + `indexed_files`/`failed_files`/`message`; added an **embedding-provider\n31\t   preflight** (`get_embedding_sync(\"ping\")`; all-zeros → 503 \"start LM Studio/Lemonade/Ollama\").\n32\t\n33\t**Phase 2 started — surfaced RAG chat.** Backend has all surfaces (server.py registers Studio/Notebook/RAG/\n34\tDeepProduce/AgentAmp/Pypes) but the Space-Agent shell only vendors a thin widget set + the Bridge cockpit\n35\t(`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js`; the rich Benny React frontend is NOT vendored — only in\n36\t`archive/benny/frontend/`). Added an \"Ask the docs\" box to the Documents panel (bridge.js `askDocs()` → POST\n37\t`/rag/chat` semantic; view.html `.ps-bridge__ask`; bridge.css). Still missing from shell: Notebook node-chat,\n38\tStudio node editor, Pypes drilldown UI, AgentAmp, Rationale-Hub wiki.\n39\t\n40\t**Arch reminder:** shell proxies `/api/runtime/*` → Benny FastAPI `127.0.0.1:8005` (`server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`,\n41\tstrips `/api/runtime`, injects `X-Benny-API-Key`). Bundled runtime started by `packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js`.\n42\t\n43\t**Self-heal + deps (2026-06-20, follow-up — \"just run the exe\").** Added `heal_collection_dimension(client,\n44\tcollection, name, probe_vec)` in `tools/knowledge.py`: canary-adds the 768-dim probe vec; on a dimensionality\n45\terror it `delete_collection` + recreates → **no manual chromadb cleanup needed**. Called in ingest right after\n46\t`get_knowledge_collection`. Confirmed the runtime bundle already bakes every ingestion dep\n47\t(`packaging/scripts/assemble-runtime-bundle.js` BUNDLE_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENTS: chromadb, PyMuPDF, pypdf,\n48\tbeautifulsoup4, markdownify; embeddings use httpx) — and since the fix routes through the HTTP\n49\t`LocalEmbeddingFunction`, **onnxruntime/sentence-transformers are NOT needed** (the old default-embedder\n50\tdownload was the bug). The ONE thing not bundlable: an external embedding/LLM server (LM Studio :1234 /\n51\tLemonade :13305 / Ollama) must be up — same prerequisite as chat/synthesis; preflight 503 says so clearly.\n52\t\n53\tCI note: prime-silo desktop gate (`release-desktop.yml`) runs only NODE tests; runtime's own\n54\t`portable-safety.yml` runs only `tests/portability tests/safety` — so `tests/api/test_rag_routes.py` does NOT\n55\tgate the exe. Tests updated anyway (success asserts indexed_files==1; +503-provider-down; +2 heal-helper unit\n56\ttests) and pass `py_compile`; not executed live (no chromadb/fastapi interpreter on this machine).\n57\t\n58\t**LIVE RUN (2026-06-20, exe) — vectors OK, synthesis was misrouting to OpenAI.** Ran ingest in the built exe\n59\t(run 08442161…, workspace default, FrolovRoutledge2024.pdf). Result: **vector ingestion WORKED** — 190 chunks\n60\tin ChromaDB (embedding fix confirmed live, local embedder reached, no onnxruntime). But the **knowledge graph\n61\tstayed empty (0 triples)**: every `graph_synthesis` LLM call failed \"Missing OPENAI_API_KEY\". Root cause = bug\n62\tin `core/models.py::get_active_model`: the local-provider heartbeat probe built the models URL via\n63\t`base_url.replace(\"/v1\",\"/models\")` which STRIPS the /v1 segment (LM Studio `:1234/v1` → `:1234/models`, a 404),\n64\tso local chat models were never detected → `default` workspace leaked to `openai/gpt-4o` (no key in bundle).\n65\tEmbeddings were unaffected (embeddings.py uses its own correct `/embeddings` path). **FIX:** probe URL =\n66\t`base_url.rstrip('/')+'/models'`; and the global fallback now stays local (`lemonade/default`) unless online\n67\tWITH an OPENAI_API_KEY. Verified LM Studio `:1234/v1/models` lists `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` → after restart the\n68\tprobe resolves `lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat`. Fix applied to source AND hot-copied into the running bundle\n69\t(`…/win-unpacked/resources/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/core/models.py`). **Runtime must be restarted (quit+relaunch\n70\tthe exe) to load it**, then re-ingest → triples should populate. NOTE: provider probe order is ollama→lemonade→\n71\tfastflowlm→lmstudio; lemonade/:13305 + ollama returned empty, lmstudio answered.\n72\t\n73\t**Agents management screen (2026-06-20) — single config surface for model routing.** User wanted Benny Studio's\n74\tagent-management screen active in the shell so all model/provider config lives in one place (not hardcoded).\n75\tBackend: `WorkspaceManifest` (core/schema.py) already has `default_model` + `model_roles` (roles: chat,\n76\tgraph_synthesis, swarm, plan, executor, tts, stt) persisted via `update_manifest`/`save_manifest` and read by\n77\t`get_active_model`. Added `GET/POST /api/llm/config` to `api/llm_routes.py` (mounts under existing `/api/llm`\n78\tprefix — no server.py change): GET returns persisted config + live `resolved` model per role + providers;\n79\tPOST writes default_model/model_roles to manifest.yaml (role=\"\" reverts to default), effective on next call,\n80\tno restart. Frontend: added an **\"Agents\" mode** to the Bridge cockpit (`app/.../bridge/bridge.js` MODES +\n81\tstate + mountAgents/loadAgents/buildModelOptions/agentProviderList/roleValue/setRoleValue/resolvedFor/saveAgents/\n82\ttoggleProvider; `view.html` panel; `bridge.css`). Lists providers (start/stop via `/api/llm/{p}/start|stop`),\n83\tshows running models, lets you set the master default + per-role model, shows what each role resolves to. Uses\n84\t`/llm/status` (provider→{running,models.data,name,port,can_start/stop}) for the model dropdowns.\n85\t\n86\tAll synced into the running exe: shell files → `…/win-unpacked/resources/app/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/`,\n87\tbackend → `…/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/api/llm_routes.py` (+ models.py earlier). Verified: node --check, py_compile,\n88\tbundled-python import of server + llm_routes endpoints OK. Runtime was DOWN at sync time (app closed, :8005 not\n89\tlistening) → loads on next exe launch. NOT yet clicked through live.\n90\t\n91\t**CRITICAL deploy fact (2026-06-20): the running app loads the runtime from the PER-USER copy\n92\t`C:\\Users\\nsdha\\AppData\\Roaming\\space-agent\\runtime-bundle\\benny\\benny\\`, NOT `win-unpacked\\resources\\runtime-bundle`.**\n93\tFirst launch extracts the bundle there (writable). To hot-patch a running exe: copy changed .py into that live\n94\tdir, clear its `__pycache__`, then `taskkill /PID <pid-on-8005> /T /F` — the \"Space Agent\" parent supervises +\n95\trelaunches the uvicorn child with fresh code. (Editing the resources copy does nothing for the running app.)\n96\t\n97\t**Full live debug chain (all fixed + verified):** (1) earlier syncs hit the wrong bundle dir → no effect.\n98\t(2) synthesis→openai/gpt-4o: fixed models.py probe URL (`base_url+\"/models\"`, not `.replace(\"/v1\",\"/models\")`)\n99\t+ local-first fallback; then PINNED via new `POST /api/llm/config` default_model=`lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat`\n100\t→ all 7 roles resolve local (also makes get_active_model fast — manifest hit skips the slow provider scan).\n101\t(3) LM Studio \"No models loaded\": embeddings hardcoded `nomic-embed-text-v1-GGUF` (Lemonade's name; Lemonade was\n102\tDOWN) → added `_resolve_embedding_model` in embeddings.py that queries provider `/models` and picks an id\n103\tcontaining \"embed\" (→ `text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5`). (4) Chroma 1.5.9 \"embedding function conflict:\n104\tpersisted: default\": old collection built with Chroma's default EF → made `get_knowledge_collection` drop+recreate\n105\ton conflict, and gave `LocalEmbeddingFunction` `name()/get_config()/build_from_config()` so future opens don't\n106\tconflict. Result: re-ingest → 190 chunks embed cleanly, NO LM Studio error, NO EF conflict.\n107\t\n108\t**REMAINING = model choice, not code. `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` is a REASONING model**: with max_tokens 1024 it\n109\temits valid triple JSON but takes ~64s for a trivial sentence (burns ~234 reasoning tokens first), and on large\n110\tdoc chunks the reasoning can exceed the budget → empty `content` (finish:length) → 0 triples → graph stays empty.\n111\tThe other LM Studio models (`qwen/qwen3-coder-30b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`) FAIL TO LOAD (\"Engine protocol startup\n112\taborted\" — memory pressure with gemma loaded). **FIX FOR USER (via the new Bridge→Agents screen):** assign\n113\t`graph_synthesis` (and `chat`) to a non-reasoning instruct model — ideally start **Lemonade** (was down) and use\n114\t**Qwen3-8B-Hybrid** (small/fast/NPU, won't fight gemma for GPU), or load a light instruct model in LM Studio.\n115\t\n116\t**Ingest \"list index out of range in add\" (Lemonade up) — empty embeddings + ChromaDB 1.5.9 strict validation.**\n117\tChromaDB 1.5.9 `validate_embeddings` rejects ANY empty vector in a batch (\"each embedding ... at least 1 value …\n118\tno values at pos N\"), failing the whole `collection.add`. `get_embedding_sync` returned `[]` when a provider\n119\tgave a 200 with no usable vector (e.g. an over-long/degenerate chunk). FIX in embeddings.py: `_extract_embedding()`\n120\tparses data[0].embedding / .embedding and returns [] only when truly absent; both sync+async now treat empty as a\n121\tprovider miss → cascade → final fallback `[0.0]*_EMBED_DIM(768)` (never empty); plus truncate inputs to\n122\t`_EMBED_MAX_CHARS=8000`. Verified: `LocalEmbeddingFunction(['x'*4000,'',...])` → all len 768. Read the live log at\n123\t`%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\logs\\api.log` to get the real traceback (my code logged only str(e)).\n124\t\n125\t**Synthesis empty output = REASONING models. `/no_think` is the fix.** User's loadable models are reasoning models:\n126\tgemma-4-12b-qat (LM Studio) and Qwen3-8B-Hybrid (Lemonade) burn the token budget \"thinking\" → empty content at\n127\tmodest max_tokens. Most other LM Studio/Lemonade models FAIL TO LOAD on this machine (memory / RyzenAI-Server /\n128\tllama-server errors) — an environment problem, not code. Qwen3 honours a **`/no_think`** directive → clean JSON\n129\ttriples in ~11s/40 tokens. FIX in core/models.py `call_model`: auto-prepend `/no_think\\n` to the last user message\n130\twhen the resolved model id contains \"qwen3\" (no effect on others). NOTE: rag_routes semantic `chat_rag` calls\n131\thttpx DIRECTLY (not call_model) so it does NOT yet get /no_think — synthesis (engine→call_model) does. Pinned\n132\tgraph_synthesis+chat+default = `lemonade/Qwen3-8B-Hybrid` via /api/llm/config.\n133\t\n134\t**\"list index out of range in add\" = lemonade nomic 512-TOKEN limit + ChromaDB 1.5.9 strict validation.** The\n135\treal cause (captured via temp EMBED-DEBUG logging of the raw provider response): lemonade's nomic-embed runs\n136\tllama-server with physical batch 512, so any input >512 tokens returns `status=200` with body\n137\t`{\"error\":{...\"input (525 tokens) is too large to process. increase the physical batch size (current batch size:512)\"}}`\n138\t→ no vector → ChromaDB 1.5.9 rejects the empty embedding → whole `collection.add` fails. Char-based truncation must\n139\tmap UNDER 512 tokens: dense/technical text ≈ 2.5-3.5 chars/tok, so **`_EMBED_MAX_CHARS = 1200`** (≤ ~480 tok, margin).\n140\t2000 chars (~525 tok) still failed. Confirmed fix live: 0 embed failures, ingest reached synthesis. (My earlier\n141\tisolation tests passed only because repeated-word text tokenizes at ~7 chars/tok.) Also: LM Studio was DOWN during\n142\tthis (only lemonade up) so there was no embedding fallback. To diagnose, log the raw 200-body, not just \"empty\".\n143\t\n144\t**GOTCHA: the bundled-runtime supervisor (`packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js`) gives up after `maxRestarts=5`.**\n145\tKilling the uvicorn child >5× in a session → supervisor stops relaunching → 8005 stays dead. To get a clean runtime\n146\twithout restarting the whole app, START IT MANUALLY (same as buildApiSpawn):\n147\t`PYTHONPATH=\"$BUNDLE/site;$BUNDLE/benny\" BENNY_HOME=%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687\n148\t$BUNDLE/python/python.exe -m uvicorn benny.api.server:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8005` (redirect 2>&1 to see logs +\n149\tEMBED-DEBUG live). Neo4j (java) keeps running independently. For the USER: just quit+relaunch the app to reset the\n150\tcounter and load latest synced code.\n151\t\n152\t**WINNING SYNTHESIS MODEL = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (NO /no_think).** Tested vs a 3200-char section: liveness 2s;\n153\tplain prompt → correct JSON triples in **12s** (~2 min for a 10-section doc); WITH /no_think → returns empty `[]`.\n154\tThis is the OPPOSITE of Qwen3-8B-Hybrid (which needed /no_think). So I REMOVED the auto-/no_think injection from\n155\tcore/models.py `call_model` (a name-substring \"qwen3\" heuristic can't distinguish the two, and it BROKE the good\n156\tmodel). Reasoning control is now left to model choice. Other small lemonade models (llama3.2-1b-FLM,\n157\tQwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-CPU, qwen3-tk-4b-FLM) return \"No model loaded\" on demand — not reliably serveable on this box;\n158\tthe big ones fail to load (RyzenAI/llama-server). Pinned graph_synthesis+default = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM`.\n159\tAlso trimmed the temp EMBED-DEBUG logging to concise warnings.\n160\t\n161\t**RELEASED v1.2.12 (2026-06-20).** Committed the 14 changed files (commit 0ec1727; logs/ + workspace/ excluded),\n162\tran `node scripts/manage-release.js patch` → v1.2.12 commit+tag, pushed main THEN tag (binary16labs/prime-silo,\n163\tgh=skybluecycology). CI release-desktop.yml run 27874230129 QUEUED → builds 6 platforms (~10-30min) + auto-publishes.\n164\tNOTE: could not run pytest release gates locally (bundled python omits pytest; no other interpreter has the deps) —\n165\trelied on py_compile/node --check + the live verification done this session.\n166\t\n167\t**Synthesis prompt-size fix (engine context overflow): default `SynthesisConfig.max_context_tokens` 4000→600\n168\t(core/schema.py) so section truncates to ~2400 chars, AND `call_llm`→`call_model` now passes `max_tokens=768`\n169\t(was call_model default 2048) — input(~860 tok: 1041-char template + 2400-char section)+output(768) ≈ 1630 tok,\n170\tfits a 2048 FLM context. Was overflowing → \"no choices\". TRIPLE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT template = ~1041 chars.\n171\t\n172\t**ROOT BLOCKER for triples is now USER INFRASTRUCTURE, not code:** (1) Neo4j is DOWN (user closed the whole app;\n173\tthe supervisor normally starts bundled neo4j.bat — no app = no Neo4j = nowhere to store triples). (2) The Lemonade\n174\tNPU server DEGRADES under sustained load — served the first ~dozen requests in 2-12s, then timed out even on a\n175\ttrivial prompt with nothing else using it. qwen3.5-9b-FLM is the best synthesis model when fresh (12s/section, real\n176\ttriples, no /no_think) but the NPU isn't stable enough for a 10-section batch. This is hardware/serving stability,\n177\tunfixable in code.\n178\t\n179\t**FINAL STATE / HANDOFF:** Document ingestion + embeddings + retrieval FULLY FIXED & verified (190 vectors;\n180\t/rag/query returns relevant passages). ALL code fixes synced to live bundle AND in `runtime/benny/` source. My\n181\tmanual runtime is STOPPED. For the graph: user must (a) RELAUNCH Space Agent (brings up Neo4j + supervised runtime\n182\twith all fixes + the qwen3.5-9b-FLM manifest config), (b) ingest ONCE on a freshly-restarted Lemonade (restart\n183\tLemonade right before to avoid the NPU-degradation), or use a more stable server (LM Studio small instruct model)\n184\tfor graph_synthesis via Bridge→Agents. Files changed this whole effort: tools/knowledge.py, core/embeddings.py,\n185\tcore/models.py, core/schema.py, api/rag_routes.py, api/llm_routes.py, synthesis/engine.py + shell bridge.js/view.html/\n186\tbridge.css. See [[project-open-studio-opencode-audit]].\n187\t\n188\t**Adaptive/agentic RAG wired into chat (2026-06-20, follow-up).** User: \"I don't like the agent not being able to\n189\tsee the file… cannot validate later\" — chose option 2 (agent decides to search, not a fixed prepend). The\n190\t`core/adaptive_rag.py` LangGraph pipeline (smart_router → retrieve single/multi-hop → grade → generate →\n191\thallucination/quality grade → rewrite loop) and `POST /api/rag/adaptive-query` already EXISTED but were unreachable\n192\tfrom the shell UI. Changes: (1) `adaptive_rag.run_adaptive_rag` model param now `Optional[str]=None` → resolves\n193\t`get_active_model(workspace, role=\"chat\")` when unpinned (local-first). (2) **Hardened `grade_documents` for the\n194\tlocal NPU**: was 1 LLM call PER doc (up to 10) → batched into ONE call returning a JSON array of relevant indices\n195\t(cap `_MAX_GRADE_DOCS=6`); anti-spiral fallback keeps top-3 retrieved docs when grading yields nothing, so a flaky\n196\tgrader can't trigger the empty→rewrite→re-retrieve death loop. (3) `api/rag_routes.py` `/rag/chat` got an\n197\t`if request.mode in (\"adaptive\",\"agent\")` branch BEFORE legacy semantic → calls run_adaptive_rag, returns\n198\tanswer+sources+route+route_explanation+execution_trace. Reads the SAME `knowledge` collection ingest writes (190\n199\tchunks confirmed via `/api/rag/status`) so PDFs are visible/validatable. (4) Shell: `bridge.js askDocs()` sends\n200\t`mode = agentMode?\"adaptive\":\"semantic\"`, captures docRoute/docTrace; added state `docRoute/docTrace/agentMode:true`;\n201\t`view.html` got an \"Agent\" checkbox + a route/trace line; `