collection.add` raised, was swallowed (rag_routes ~line 180), and the endpoint\n   still returned `status:\"completed\"` → hollow success, empty index. Plus 384-vs-768 dim mismatch when\n   tool + route paths touched the same collection.\n   **FIX:** added `get_knowledge_collection(client, name=\"knowledge\")` in `tools/knowledge.py` (always\n   attaches `LocalEmbeddingFunction()`); routed ALL call sites through it. `grep 'get_or_create_collection(\"knowledge\")'`\n   must return nothing.\n2. **No triples → empty graph.** Documents page's kg3d/synoptic_web reads Neo4j (`graph/kg3d/ontology.py`),\n   populated only by `deep_synthesis` (triple extraction). But Bridge `ingest()` posted `{workspace}` and\n   `deep_synthesis` defaults False → graph stayed empty though the chip promises triples.\n   **FIX:** `bridge.js ingest()` now sends `deep_synthesis:true`.\n3. **Silent failure.** Indexing/synthesis errors caught + reported as success.\n   **FIX:** ingest tracks per-file `indexed`/`error`, returns honest `status` ∈ completed /\n   completed_with_errors / failed + `indexed_files`/`failed_files`/`message`; added an **embedding-provider\n   preflight** (`get_embedding_sync(\"ping\")`; all-zeros → 503 \"start LM Studio/Lemonade/Ollama\").\n\n**Phase 2 started — surfaced RAG chat.** Backend has all surfaces (server.py registers Studio/Notebook/RAG/\nDeepProduce/AgentAmp/Pypes) but the Space-Agent shell only vendors a thin widget set + the Bridge cockpit\n(`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js`; the rich Benny React frontend is NOT vendored — only in\n`archive/benny/frontend/`). Added an \"Ask the docs\" box to the Documents panel (bridge.js `askDocs()` → POST\n`/rag/chat` semantic; view.html `.ps-bridge__ask`; bridge.css). Still missing from shell: Notebook node-chat,\nStudio node editor, Pypes drilldown UI, AgentAmp, Rationale-Hub wiki.\n\n**Arch reminder:** shell proxies `/api/runtime/*` → Benny FastAPI `127.0.0.1:8005` (`server/lib/runtime_proxy.js`,\nstrips `/api/runtime`, injects `X-Benny-API-Key`). Bundled runtime started by `packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js`.\n\n**Self-heal + deps (2026-06-20, follow-up — \"just run the exe\").** Added `heal_collection_dimension(client,\ncollection, name, probe_vec)` in `tools/knowledge.py`: canary-adds the 768-dim probe vec; on a dimensionality\nerror it `delete_collection` + recreates → **no manual chromadb cleanup needed**. Called in ingest right after\n`get_knowledge_collection`. Confirmed the runtime bundle already bakes every ingestion dep\n(`packaging/scripts/assemble-runtime-bundle.js` BUNDLE_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENTS: chromadb, PyMuPDF, pypdf,\nbeautifulsoup4, markdownify; embeddings use httpx) — and since the fix routes through the HTTP\n`LocalEmbeddingFunction`, **onnxruntime/sentence-transformers are NOT needed** (the old default-embedder\ndownload was the bug). The ONE thing not bundlable: an external embedding/LLM server (LM Studio :1234 /\nLemonade :13305 / Ollama) must be up — same prerequisite as chat/synthesis; preflight 503 says so clearly.\n\nCI note: prime-silo desktop gate (`release-desktop.yml`) runs only NODE tests; runtime's own\n`portable-safety.yml` runs only `tests/portability tests/safety` — so `tests/api/test_rag_routes.py` does NOT\ngate the exe. Tests updated anyway (success asserts indexed_files==1; +503-provider-down; +2 heal-helper unit\ntests) and pass `py_compile`; not executed live (no chromadb/fastapi interpreter on this machine).\n\n**LIVE RUN (2026-06-20, exe) — vectors OK, synthesis was misrouting to OpenAI.** Ran ingest in the built exe\n(run 08442161…, workspace default, FrolovRoutledge2024.pdf). Result: **vector ingestion WORKED** — 190 chunks\nin ChromaDB (embedding fix confirmed live, local embedder reached, no onnxruntime). But the **knowledge graph\nstayed empty (0 triples)**: every `graph_synthesis` LLM call failed \"Missing OPENAI_API_KEY\". Root cause = bug\nin `core/models.py::get_active_model`: the local-provider heartbeat probe built the models URL via\n`base_url.replace(\"/v1\",\"/models\")` which STRIPS the /v1 segment (LM Studio `:1234/v1` → `:1234/models`, a 404),\nso local chat models were never detected → `default` workspace leaked to `openai/gpt-4o` (no key in bundle).\nEmbeddings were unaffected (embeddings.py uses its own correct `/embeddings` path). **FIX:** probe URL =\n`base_url.rstrip('/')+'/models'`; and the global fallback now stays local (`lemonade/default`) unless online\nWITH an OPENAI_API_KEY. Verified LM Studio `:1234/v1/models` lists `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` → after restart the\nprobe resolves `lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat`. Fix applied to source AND hot-copied into the running bundle\n(`…/win-unpacked/resources/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/core/models.py`). **Runtime must be restarted (quit+relaunch\nthe exe) to load it**, then re-ingest → triples should populate. NOTE: provider probe order is ollama→lemonade→\nfastflowlm→lmstudio; lemonade/:13305 + ollama returned empty, lmstudio answered.\n\n**Agents management screen (2026-06-20) — single config surface for model routing.** User wanted Benny Studio's\nagent-management screen active in the shell so all model/provider config lives in one place (not hardcoded).\nBackend: `WorkspaceManifest` (core/schema.py) already has `default_model` + `model_roles` (roles: chat,\ngraph_synthesis, swarm, plan, executor, tts, stt) persisted via `update_manifest`/`save_manifest` and read by\n`get_active_model`. Added `GET/POST /api/llm/config` to `api/llm_routes.py` (mounts under existing `/api/llm`\nprefix — no server.py change): GET returns persisted config + live `resolved` model per role + providers;\nPOST writes default_model/model_roles to manifest.yaml (role=\"\" reverts to default), effective on next call,\nno restart. Frontend: added an **\"Agents\" mode** to the Bridge cockpit (`app/.../bridge/bridge.js` MODES +\nstate + mountAgents/loadAgents/buildModelOptions/agentProviderList/roleValue/setRoleValue/resolvedFor/saveAgents/\ntoggleProvider; `view.html` panel; `bridge.css`). Lists providers (start/stop via `/api/llm/{p}/start|stop`),\nshows running models, lets you set the master default + per-role model, shows what each role resolves to. Uses\n`/llm/status` (provider→{running,models.data,name,port,can_start/stop}) for the model dropdowns.\n\nAll synced into the running exe: shell files → `…/win-unpacked/resources/app/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/`,\nbackend → `…/runtime-bundle/benny/benny/api/llm_routes.py` (+ models.py earlier). Verified: node --check, py_compile,\nbundled-python import of server + llm_routes endpoints OK. Runtime was DOWN at sync time (app closed, :8005 not\nlistening) → loads on next exe launch. NOT yet clicked through live.\n\n**CRITICAL deploy fact (2026-06-20): the running app loads the runtime from the PER-USER copy\n`C:\\Users\\nsdha\\AppData\\Roaming\\space-agent\\runtime-bundle\\benny\\benny\\`, NOT `win-unpacked\\resources\\runtime-bundle`.**\nFirst launch extracts the bundle there (writable). To hot-patch a running exe: copy changed .py into that live\ndir, clear its `__pycache__`, then `taskkill /PID <pid-on-8005> /T /F` — the \"Space Agent\" parent supervises +\nrelaunches the uvicorn child with fresh code. (Editing the resources copy does nothing for the running app.)\n\n**Full live debug chain (all fixed + verified):** (1) earlier syncs hit the wrong bundle dir → no effect.\n(2) synthesis→openai/gpt-4o: fixed models.py probe URL (`base_url+\"/models\"`, not `.replace(\"/v1\",\"/models\")`)\n+ local-first fallback; then PINNED via new `POST /api/llm/config` default_model=`lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b-qat`\n→ all 7 roles resolve local (also makes get_active_model fast — manifest hit skips the slow provider scan).\n(3) LM Studio \"No models loaded\": embeddings hardcoded `nomic-embed-text-v1-GGUF` (Lemonade's name; Lemonade was\nDOWN) → added `_resolve_embedding_model` in embeddings.py that queries provider `/models` and picks an id\ncontaining \"embed\" (→ `text-embedding-nomic-embed-text-v1.5`). (4) Chroma 1.5.9 \"embedding function conflict:\npersisted: default\": old collection built with Chroma's default EF → made `get_knowledge_collection` drop+recreate\non conflict, and gave `LocalEmbeddingFunction` `name()/get_config()/build_from_config()` so future opens don't\nconflict. Result: re-ingest → 190 chunks embed cleanly, NO LM Studio error, NO EF conflict.\n\n**REMAINING = model choice, not code. `google/gemma-4-12b-qat` is a REASONING model**: with max_tokens 1024 it\nemits valid triple JSON but takes ~64s for a trivial sentence (burns ~234 reasoning tokens first), and on large\ndoc chunks the reasoning can exceed the budget → empty `content` (finish:length) → 0 triples → graph stays empty.\nThe other LM Studio models (`qwen/qwen3-coder-30b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`) FAIL TO LOAD (\"Engine protocol startup\naborted\" — memory pressure with gemma loaded). **FIX FOR USER (via the new Bridge→Agents screen):** assign\n`graph_synthesis` (and `chat`) to a non-reasoning instruct model — ideally start **Lemonade** (was down) and use\n**Qwen3-8B-Hybrid** (small/fast/NPU, won't fight gemma for GPU), or load a light instruct model in LM Studio.\n\n**Ingest \"list index out of range in add\" (Lemonade up) — empty embeddings + ChromaDB 1.5.9 strict validation.**\nChromaDB 1.5.9 `validate_embeddings` rejects ANY empty vector in a batch (\"each embedding ... at least 1 value …\nno values at pos N\"), failing the whole `collection.add`. `get_embedding_sync` returned `[]` when a provider\ngave a 200 with no usable vector (e.g. an over-long/degenerate chunk). FIX in embeddings.py: `_extract_embedding()`\nparses data[0].embedding / .embedding and returns [] only when truly absent; both sync+async now treat empty as a\nprovider miss → cascade → final fallback `[0.0]*_EMBED_DIM(768)` (never empty); plus truncate inputs to\n`_EMBED_MAX_CHARS=8000`. Verified: `LocalEmbeddingFunction(['x'*4000,'',...])` → all len 768. Read the live log at\n`%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\logs\\api.log` to get the real traceback (my code logged only str(e)).\n\n**Synthesis empty output = REASONING models. `/no_think` is the fix.** User's loadable models are reasoning models:\ngemma-4-12b-qat (LM Studio) and Qwen3-8B-Hybrid (Lemonade) burn the token budget \"thinking\" → empty content at\nmodest max_tokens. Most other LM Studio/Lemonade models FAIL TO LOAD on this machine (memory / RyzenAI-Server /\nllama-server errors) — an environment problem, not code. Qwen3 honours a **`/no_think`** directive → clean JSON\ntriples in ~11s/40 tokens. FIX in core/models.py `call_model`: auto-prepend `/no_think\\n` to the last user message\nwhen the resolved model id contains \"qwen3\" (no effect on others). NOTE: rag_routes semantic `chat_rag` calls\nhttpx DIRECTLY (not call_model) so it does NOT yet get /no_think — synthesis (engine→call_model) does. Pinned\ngraph_synthesis+chat+default = `lemonade/Qwen3-8B-Hybrid` via /api/llm/config.\n\n**\"list index out of range in add\" = lemonade nomic 512-TOKEN limit + ChromaDB 1.5.9 strict validation.** The\nreal cause (captured via temp EMBED-DEBUG logging of the raw provider response): lemonade's nomic-embed runs\nllama-server with physical batch 512, so any input >512 tokens returns `status=200` with body\n`{\"error\":{...\"input (525 tokens) is too large to process. increase the physical batch size (current batch size:512)\"}}`\n→ no vector → ChromaDB 1.5.9 rejects the empty embedding → whole `collection.add` fails. Char-based truncation must\nmap UNDER 512 tokens: dense/technical text ≈ 2.5-3.5 chars/tok, so **`_EMBED_MAX_CHARS = 1200`** (≤ ~480 tok, margin).\n2000 chars (~525 tok) still failed. Confirmed fix live: 0 embed failures, ingest reached synthesis. (My earlier\nisolation tests passed only because repeated-word text tokenizes at ~7 chars/tok.) Also: LM Studio was DOWN during\nthis (only lemonade up) so there was no embedding fallback. To diagnose, log the raw 200-body, not just \"empty\".\n\n**GOTCHA: the bundled-runtime supervisor (`packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js`) gives up after `maxRestarts=5`.**\nKilling the uvicorn child >5× in a session → supervisor stops relaunching → 8005 stays dead. To get a clean runtime\nwithout restarting the whole app, START IT MANUALLY (same as buildApiSpawn):\n`PYTHONPATH=\"$BUNDLE/site;$BUNDLE/benny\" BENNY_HOME=%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687\n$BUNDLE/python/python.exe -m uvicorn benny.api.server:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8005` (redirect 2>&1 to see logs +\nEMBED-DEBUG live). Neo4j (java) keeps running independently. For the USER: just quit+relaunch the app to reset the\ncounter and load latest synced code.\n\n**WINNING SYNTHESIS MODEL = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (NO /no_think).** Tested vs a 3200-char section: liveness 2s;\nplain prompt → correct JSON triples in **12s** (~2 min for a 10-section doc); WITH /no_think → returns empty `[]`.\nThis is the OPPOSITE of Qwen3-8B-Hybrid (which needed /no_think). So I REMOVED the auto-/no_think injection from\ncore/models.py `call_model` (a name-substring \"qwen3\" heuristic can't distinguish the two, and it BROKE the good\nmodel). Reasoning control is now left to model choice. Other small lemonade models (llama3.2-1b-FLM,\nQwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-CPU, qwen3-tk-4b-FLM) return \"No model loaded\" on demand — not reliably serveable on this box;\nthe big ones fail to load (RyzenAI/llama-server). Pinned graph_synthesis+default = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM`.\nAlso trimmed the temp EMBED-DEBUG logging to concise warnings.\n\n**RELEASED v1.2.12 (2026-06-20).** Committed the 14 changed files (commit 0ec1727; logs/ + workspace/ excluded),\nran `node scripts/manage-release.js patch` → v1.2.12 commit+tag, pushed main THEN tag (binary16labs/prime-silo,\ngh=skybluecycology). CI release-desktop.yml run 27874230129 QUEUED → builds 6 platforms (~10-30min) + auto-publishes.\nNOTE: could not run pytest release gates locally (bundled python omits pytest; no other interpreter has the deps) —\nrelied on py_compile/node --check + the live verification done this session.\n\n**Synthesis prompt-size fix (engine context overflow): default `SynthesisConfig.max_context_tokens` 4000→600\n(core/schema.py) so section truncates to ~2400 chars, AND `call_llm`→`call_model` now passes `max_tokens=768`\n(was call_model default 2048) — input(~860 tok: 1041-char template + 2400-char section)+output(768) ≈ 1630 tok,\nfits a 2048 FLM context. Was overflowing → \"no choices\". TRIPLE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT template = ~1041 chars.\n\n**ROOT BLOCKER for triples is now USER INFRASTRUCTURE, not code:** (1) Neo4j is DOWN (user closed the whole app;\nthe supervisor normally starts bundled neo4j.bat — no app = no Neo4j = nowhere to store triples). (2) The Lemonade\nNPU server DEGRADES under sustained load — served the first ~dozen requests in 2-12s, then timed out even on a\ntrivial prompt with nothing else using it. qwen3.5-9b-FLM is the best synthesis model when fresh (12s/section, real\ntriples, no /no_think) but the NPU isn't stable enough for a 10-section batch. This is hardware/serving stability,\nunfixable in code.\n\n**FINAL STATE / HANDOFF:** Document ingestion + embeddings + retrieval FULLY FIXED & verified (190 vectors;\n/rag/query returns relevant passages). ALL code fixes synced to live bundle AND in `runtime/benny/` source. My\nmanual runtime is STOPPED. For the graph: user must (a) RELAUNCH Space Agent (brings up Neo4j + supervised runtime\nwith all fixes + the qwen3.5-9b-FLM manifest config), (b) ingest ONCE on a freshly-restarted Lemonade (restart\nLemonade right before to avoid the NPU-degradation), or use a more stable server (LM Studio small instruct model)\nfor graph_synthesis via Bridge→Agents. Files changed this whole effort: tools/knowledge.py, core/embeddings.py,\ncore/models.py, core/schema.py, api/rag_routes.py, api/llm_routes.py, synthesis/engine.py + shell bridge.js/view.html/\nbridge.css. See [[project-open-studio-opencode-audit]].\n\n**Adaptive/agentic RAG wired into chat (2026-06-20, follow-up).** User: \"I don't like the agent not being able to\nsee the file… cannot validate later\" — chose option 2 (agent decides to search, not a fixed prepend). The\n`core/adaptive_rag.py` LangGraph pipeline (smart_router → retrieve single/multi-hop → grade → generate →\nhallucination/quality grade → rewrite loop) and `POST /api/rag/adaptive-query` already EXISTED but were unreachable\nfrom the shell UI. Changes: (1) `adaptive_rag.run_adaptive_rag` model param now `Optional[str]=None` → resolves\n`get_active_model(workspace, role=\"chat\")` when unpinned (local-first). (2) **Hardened `grade_documents` for the\nlocal NPU**: was 1 LLM call PER doc (up to 10) → batched into ONE call returning a JSON array of relevant indices\n(cap `_MAX_GRADE_DOCS=6`); anti-spiral fallback keeps top-3 retrieved docs when grading yields nothing, so a flaky\ngrader can't trigger the empty→rewrite→re-retrieve death loop. (3) `api/rag_routes.py` `/rag/chat` got an\n`if request.mode in (\"adaptive\",\"agent\")` branch BEFORE legacy semantic → calls run_adaptive_rag, returns\nanswer+sources+route+route_explanation+execution_trace. Reads the SAME `knowledge` collection ingest writes (190\nchunks confirmed via `/api/rag/status`) so PDFs are visible/validatable. (4) Shell: `bridge.js askDocs()` sends\n`mode = agentMode?\"adaptive\":\"semantic\"`, captures docRoute/docTrace; added state `docRoute/docTrace/agentMode:true`;\n`view.html` got an \"Agent\" checkbox + a route/trace line; `bridge.css` `.ps-bridge__ask-toggle/.ps-bridge__ask-route`.\nSynced to live bundle `…\\runtime-bundle\\benny\\benny\\{core/adaptive_rag,api/rag_routes}.py`; py_compile + node --check\npass. **NOT yet smoke-tested live — runtime has old code in memory (no --reload); user must quit+relaunch Space Agent\n(or I restart the uvicorn child) to load it.** Then: Documents panel → \"Ask the docs\" with Agent on. NOTE the legacy\nnotebook chat (`api/chat_routes.py`) STILL reads the wrong `notebook_<id>` collection (option 1, not done) — only\n`/rag/chat` is fixed.\n\n**Per-file ingest selection (2026-06-20, follow-up).** User couldn't choose WHICH doc to ingest; rescan showed \"2\nawaiting ingestion\" with no way to pick. ROOT CAUSE = pure frontend: the Documents file list (`view.html`\n`.ps-bridge__files-list`) rendered read-only rows (name+status), and the single `ingest()` posted\n`{workspace,deep_synthesis:true}` with **no `files` array** → backend `rag_routes.py` ingest globs ALL of\n`data_in` (`if request.files: … else: data_in_path.glob(\"*.*\")`). Backend ALREADY supported a subset via\n`IngestRequest.files: List[str]` (filenames joined `data_in_path / f`) — only the UI never sent it. (\"2 awaiting\" =\n`pendingCount` = files with status≠ALIGNED; that count was correct, just unusable.) FIX (frontend only): added\n`selectedFiles:[]` state + `reconcileSelection()` (prunes stale, default-selects pending non-ALIGNED so \"ingest the\ndoc I just added\" is one click) called at end of `loadFiles()`; `isSelected/toggleFile/selectAllFiles/\nclearFileSelection`; `ingest()` now builds `targets` from selection, guards empty (\"Select at least one…\"), posts\n`files: targets`. view.html: per-row checkbox (`.ps-bridge__file-pick`), Select all/None tools, header shows\n`· N selected`, button = `Ingest selected (N)` disabled when 0. bridge.css: pick/tools styles. node --check OK;\nsynced to both exes' `resources/app/...bridge/`. File obj shape from `mergeFileStatus` = `{name,status,chunks,type}`\n(no path) — selection keyed by `name`, matches backend. Not committed/released yet.\n\n**Per-model thinking toggle in Agents screen (2026-06-20, follow-up).** User wanted a per-model think/no-think\ntoggle (e.g. run gemma-4-12b-qat WITHOUT thinking). This is the EXPLICIT replacement for the removed name-substring\n/no_think heuristic — qwen3.5-9b-FLM needs thinking ON (empty WITH /no_think), Qwen3-8B-Hybrid/gemma want it OFF.\nMechanism when a model is set 'off': `call_model` injects `/no_think\\n` into the last user msg AND passes\n`chat_template_kwargs:{enable_thinking:false}` via `extra_body` — the two standard switches; whether honored is\nchat-template-dependent (best-effort for gemma). Files: (1) `core/schema.py` WorkspaceManifest +`model_thinking:\nDict[str,str]` ('provider/model'→'on'|'off'). (2) `core/local_executor.py` `BaseOpenAICompatibleExecutor.generate`\nmerges a new `extra_body` kwarg dict into the OpenAI payload. (3) `core/models.py`: new `_thinking_disabled(model,\nactual_model,workspace_id)` reads manifest.model_thinking; in `call_model` section \"2b\" (after augmentation) builds\n`think_extra` + prepends /no_think when off; passes `extra_body=think_extra` to executor.generate (local path) and\n`kwargs[\"extra_body\"]=think_extra` (litellm path). Single injection point so both paths inherit. (4)\n`api/llm_routes.py`: ModelConfigRequest +`model_thinking`; GET /config returns it; POST merges (only 'off' persists,\n'on'/'' clears → model default). (5) shell `bridge.js`: `thinkingOff(v)`/`toggleThinking(v)` helpers, saveAgents\nposts `model_thinking`; `view.html` Agents wide-col new \"Reasoning (thinking)\" block — a checkbox per\n`agentModelOptions` model (checked=thinking on); `bridge.css` `.ps-bridge__thinking/.ps-bridge__think-row/-name/-state`.\nEffective next call, no restart (manifest-read). py_compile+node --check OK; synced to live per-user bundle + both\nexes' resources + win-unpacked runtime-bundle. Runtime needs relaunch to load (old code in memory). Not committed/released.\n\n**`desktop:localtest` build delivery mechanism (2026-06-20, learned).** Ran `npm run desktop:localtest` (build-local-\ntest.js, sets PRIME_SILO_BUNDLE_RUNTIME=1) → built `dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe` (192MB,\nelectron only). KEY: the **runtime bundle is NOT shipped inside the exe** — `resources/` has only `app` + default_app.asar,\nno `runtime-bund