t effect once you're on v1.4.7\nYou've now got a stack of fixes landing together — staging→ingest (v1.4.5), graph connectivity + hierarchy (v1.4.6), and triple-parse recovery (v1.4.7). The practical impact: more of each document's triples survive extraction, so the graph will be **denser and better connected**, on top of the layout fixes.\n\nOne honest caveat: mode 2 (markdown non-compliance) is a model-behavior problem. The stricter prompt reduces it, but `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` may still occasionally drift. If you keep seeing sparse graphs, the higher-leverage lever is the synthesis model choice itself — but the parser is now as forgiving as it safely can be. Update to v1.4.7 (relaunch → runtime re-fetches) to pick all this up."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1248,"cache_read_input_tokens":369432,"output_tokens":981,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1248,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":981,"cache_read_input_tokens":369432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1248},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcVXQayrUAtSPDdGuk9yN","type":"assistant","uuid":"14fe9b46-682b-4dc4-8620-8832bf9b91e7","timestamp":"2026-06-28T10:47:40.281Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"b5bb1984-4ef6-4dd6-8984-6e589fd772ec","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
